Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface_contract::verification::the_handoff_round_trips`.

The defect: `Handoff::unpack` stops requiring the register mask to include page 0. A kernel bug (or
a hostile spawn word) that maps no capability-register page is then accepted, and the driver's first
read faults.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(h.registers & 1 != 0)`: `unpack` accepted a mask without page 0.

diff --git a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -90,7 +90,6 @@
         let ok = w[0] != 0
             && w[0].is_multiple_of(PAGE_BYTES)
             && u64::from(dma_pages) >= WORK_PAGES
-            && registers & 1 != 0
             && w[2] == 0;
         ok.then_some(Handoff {
